  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-50 (not deemed medically necessary), which is a substantive denial rather than a coding or administrative error, so resubmitting the same data (submit_clean) or fixing codes (correct_and_resubmit) will not resolve the medical necessity issue. The payer does not offer peer-to-peer review, and retroactive authorization is not available, leaving a formal appeal as the only viable path to challenge the medical necessity determination. Historical data shows that while appeals have a mixed success rate, they are the standard and only appropriate mechanism for overturning a CO-50 denial in this context.",
